00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:56,790
It's what I call the Clever Hans effect.

505
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:58,910
You heard of Clever Hans?

506
00:41:58,910 --> 00:42:02,670
This was a horse at the beginning of the 20th century.

507
00:42:02,670 --> 00:42:07,110
A horse in Germany that apparently could do arithmetic and read maps and do all sorts of stuff.

508
00:42:07,110 --> 00:42:11,510
And so he toured all these fairs and the great and the good came to see Clever Hans.

509
00:42:11,520 --> 00:42:13,950
And his trainer would say, what's 6 * 9?

510
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:17,550
Clever hands would tap it out with his hoof, and so on and so forth.

511
00:42:17,550 --> 00:42:23,750
People were amazed, but there were some skeptics, and the skeptics, they organized some experiments, tests.

512
00:42:23,750 --> 00:42:27,750
And in some of the tests, the horse couldn't see his trainer.

513
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:31,710
He was blinkered, and when the horse couldn't see his trainer, he got all the answers wrong.

514
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:34,070
So, there must have been something happening in there.

515
00:42:34,080 --> 00:42:40,550
The trainer, probably totally unconsciously, was somehow signaling visually to the horse what to do.

516
00:42:40,550 --> 00:42:43,110
And I've seen people do that with LLMs.

517
00:42:43,110 --> 00:42:49,190
I've seen I've watched them step in, fix things, correct things, and at the end go, "See, it did it all."

